Subject: Driver::poll_received, a turn's events before its sends
Why: An owner that passes what comes in onward waited for each turn's sends before the turn's first event: Driver::poll_event takes what arrived, sends, then hands out. poll_received is the same turn split at that seam, an event the receive half made handed out before the send half, which the caller makes with flush in the same turn (its doc says what it owes, and what holding it costs the peer's round trip and congestion window); poll_event is built from the same pieces and does what it did. kiln's net thread hands a turn's frames to its shards before the turn's sends (kiln's goal 10, plan 01a1a87b2dae step 5). Offered upstream; no other caller calls it

